          "id": "SP_AMPHIANTHUS_BATHYBIUM_HERTWIG_1882",
          "name": "Amphianthus bathybium Hertwig, 1882",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Amphianthus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "SHORT DESCRIPTION. Individuals 5.6 to 8.7 mm in height and 16.6 to 24.1 mm in diameter. Number of tentacles corresponds to the number of mesenteries: 48 pairs of mesenteries and 48 tentacles arranged in four cycles. Most of the sampled specimens were attached to Acanella sp. and branches of Chrysogorgia tuberculata Cordeiro, Castro & Pérez, 2015. CNIDOM. Spirocysts, basitrichs, holotrichs, and microbasic p - mastigophores B 1 (Fig. 4 I: a – e, Table 3).",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:5184283",
